From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] retain same-build resolver TLS dependency closure in M4 APEX

# Reason: attempt0209 logcat_live.txt:54555 reports netd cannot load libcrypto.so from the tethering namespace; libnetd_resolv also requires libssl.so. Both are private DSOs present in the same hash-pinned BZI6 APEX but absent in the S22 base.
# Affected: diagnostic M4 network APEX composition helper and output/input lock. Add only BZI6 lib64/libcrypto.so and lib64/libssl.so beside its resolver; preserve namespace exports and both matching manifests.
# Verify: pin all three resolver DSO hashes; recursively require DT_NEEDED to resolve inside the APEX or through an explicit manifest import; check payload file allowlist, UID/GID/mode/SELinux, ext4 roundtrip, AVB, v3, alignment and repeatable output. Static resolver symbol/version closure covers 23 DSOs; device runtime remains a separate gate.
# Rollback: restore the byte-verified attempt0209 APEX backup and reverse0210; no kernel/vendor/radio/protected-partition change.

